          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105165",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=2$, which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8(2) & =-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =15 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & =-2 \\\\ -2(5)+4(2) & =-2 \\\\ -2 & =-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5+2=7.\n$$"
